Annotate the Blocks runtime pointer bounds.

Source: libdispatch-1542.100.32 (701f4d1a24ae9c6863901bbbb22624b7d1b87321),
src/BlocksRuntime/Block.h. Scope: macOS SDK 26.5, arm64 and x86_64.

The pinned licensed header needs a single-pointer boundary for raw copy
and release under Clang bounds safety. Use Clang's documented annotations
and forge operation in the typed wrappers, retaining the upstream notice.
The fixture checks valid single-pointer copy and rejection of unsafe raw
release. Ordinary C clients emitted identical objects.

Evidence: https://clang.llvm.org/docs/BoundsSafety.html
